/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/21897d95/D5/2/code.py:329:    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker still indicates a 90-degree output rotation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/2/code.py:17:#   - The visible objects stay the same as the original task: isolated border anchors,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/2/code.py:19:#   - The changed behavior is purely in the translation amount. For a top-edge anchor
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/2/code.py:30:#   - To keep the midpoint effect visible, generation enforces abs(anchor-midpoint) >= 2.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/2/code.py:31:#     Then the input-anchor gap is at least 4, so the output is clearly not the old
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/2/code.py:33:#   - Multiple sprites can still share one anchor color, preserving repeated evidence.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D14/2/code.py:39:#     input positions by reflection: input = 2 * midpoint - anchor.
